Flood Warning is extended for the following rivers in\nColorado...\n\nRio Grande At Alamosa affecting Alamosa County.\n\nFor the Upper Rio Grande...including Alamosa...Minor flooding is\nforecast.\n\n* WHAT...Minor flooding is occurring and minor flooding is forecast.\n\n* WHERE...Rio Grande at Alamosa.\n\n* WHEN...Until Tuesday evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...At 9.0 feet, Minor flooding. Minor agricultural flooding\nin low lying areas along the river\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 9:30 PM MDT Monday the stage was 9.3 feet.\n- Bankfull stage is 7.0 feet.\n- Recent Activity...The maximum river stage in the 24 hours ending\nat 9:30 PM MDT Monday was 9.7 feet.\n- Forecast...The river is expected to fall to 4 feet by 1 pm Monday\nafternoon.\n- Flood stage is 9.0 feet.\n- Flood History...This crest compares to a previous crest of 9.3\nfeet on 05/18/1944.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-27T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Alamosa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e27af4daa3f329caea6e29353ef1555aeaede94b.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e27af4daa3f329caea6e29353ef1555aeaede94b.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Warning","headline":"Flood Warning issued October 25 at 11:43PM MDT until October 27 at 12:45AM MDT by NWS Pueblo CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Southeastern Rio Grande County in south central Colorado...\nWest Central Alamosa County in southeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 1245 AM MDT Tuesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is imminent or occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1141 PM MDT, Gauge reports indicated high stream flows.\nFlooding is already occurring in the warned area.\n- Widespread inundation of agriculture fields, wetlands, and other\nlow-lying areas.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nMainly rural areas of Southeastern Rio Grande an